    "recommendations": "• Thin trees within the scattered clusters closest to the structure to reduce the amount of vegetation that could carry fire toward the building.\n• Trim or remove shrubs growing directly against or immediately next to the structure.\n• Cut grass near the structure and around outbuildings short, especially during dry periods.\n• Clear overhanging branches and shrubs along the driveway to keep the travel lane fully open for vehicles.\n• Separate shrubs from the base of the structure by removing those within a few feet of the foundation or walls.\n• Remove dead or dry grass and plant material from the open green space areas closest to the structure.\n• Thin scattered shrubs between tree clusters and the structure to reduce the amount of connected vegetation between them.\n• Keep the area under tree clusters near the structure clear of low-hanging branches and accumulated dead material on the ground.\n• Maintain the existing separation between vegetation and the structure by trimming back any plants that are beginning to close that gap."
